Package: auxiv
Type: Package
Title: Auxiliary Instrumental Variable Estimation for Nonlinear Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Riccardo", "D'Adamo", email = "r.dadamo@econ.au.dk",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Martin", "Weidner", role = "aut"),
    person("Frank", "Windmeijer", role = "aut"))
Description: Implements the Auxiliary Instrumental Variable (AIV) estimator of
    D'Adamo, Weidner and Windmeijer for non-linear models with endogenous
    covariates. The instruments are added to the model as auxiliary
    regressors and the structural coefficients are chosen so that the
    estimated auxiliary coefficients are close to zero. The estimator is
    consistent when the coefficients on the endogenous regressors are zero
    and is locally sign consistent, without imposing any functional form or
    distributional assumption on the first stage. Supports the binary choice
    (probit, logit, cloglog) and Poisson cases via the standard 'family'
    interface, and provides standard errors valid under over-identification.
    Also provides the Rivers-Vuong control function estimator for comparison,
    with standard errors that correct for estimation of the first stage and
    with a choice of normalisation of the structural error variance.
URL: https://github.com/rdadamo/auxiliaryIV
BugReports: https://github.com/rdadamo/auxiliaryIV/issues
